te]} {:db/id "q-71888" :question/id #uuid "78d4d1dd-aca2-5029-99b9-a7becab58e6c" :question/math-academy-id "q-71888" :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0\\le {x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<4,\\,0\\le y<2}.\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,,\\,0<y<2}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072304/assets/f4ee8fbf9a7670a7d0e0b7488bccbf014f8db8fff0154c7db025f2b071aec566.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072304/assets/9fc733f6966b016c93b6ee6a305c5af5ee4fa432dad5d95e28061fd2a0d33efb.png)\n\nSo, in this case, the interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0<{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<4,\\,0<y<2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-71888/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f89386f9-8a2b-56eb-8521-7c1ddafcfd96"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-71888"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-161596/selection/3b25e84be09f9e3d706cd9b661f217237b44dd9fca4190c6f72a583105e8fbc8" :answer/id #uuid "48563982-89ee-5bb8-baec-cb82cd3e7083" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}<-x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161596/selection/fe85096b3987d33f82bed6ac26bd9023c11210c3fca79130614988dcba307bb5" :answer/id #uuid "161a53b4-89a7-59b6-909e-b03278987160" :answer