.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072304/assets/88f35519cf1aa01bcc9e4fb91b24c2bc2a1a823867ec2670563b0b45f2643a0a.png)\n\nFrom the diagram, the boundary points of $A$ lie on the parabola ${y}^{2}=-x.$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n∂A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{y}^{2}=-x\\,}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-161596/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e534c006-a5b4-5f76-bbd6-451496358d3a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161596"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-161601/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "adcf6414-1d3e-5c51-825c-39866b51f27e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161601/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "322b662e-5404-5635-aee4-3ab77363404f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161601/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "b648d80f-658d-5211-87f3-e39e80415e4b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161601/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "4ed70b02-733f-5eae-8f02-c7c64dc01c85" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161601/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "e172786e-070e-5772-87e4-cb0f67273db7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161601/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "85322f6b-516f-5402-8c45-cb902ded5ab9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-161601/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer-field/choices ["q-161601/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-161601/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-161601/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-161601/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-161601/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-161601" :question/id #uuid "84f3ca08-8934-5cbf-812e-630649f3de0f" :question/math-academy-id "q-161601" :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}<36}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $A$ contains none of its boundary points.\n- $A$ contains some (not all) of its boundary points.\n- $\\text{int}\\,A=A$" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nIn this case, the set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072304/assets/ff1f735266f66879834e02ca7601e90e40dfa7929e5796d4a3f8cb4ff2828de7.png)\n\n  \n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nNotice that, in this case, the set $A$ contains none of its boundary points. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true, while statement II is false. As we've seen, $A$ contains none of its boundary points.\n\n- Statement III is true. Since $A$ contains none of its boundary points, we must have $\\text{int}\\,A=A.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-161601/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a024c46e-0374-5d03-b895-eb754ff7ad97"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161601"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-161652/selection/061c0582fe9c4fc8f6a2754ba48c864a097431d239f9b07d7f28c26670db035c" :answer/id #uuid "a3d796fa-a51e-50a8-8acc-fedc48733837" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III  only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161652/selection/f875651f7f1318c0bb7eec422091a285a478534fed6eb95898ab3cf27eb909ff" :answer/id #uuid "b878bb07-2cb0-5f66-a06f-838dc9fcfcce" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III  only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161652/selection/18f1ea50d5b97ea6ddf4ed047cc851740c3854be5650eb9e76df7f5a3d1456f8" :answer/id #uuid "281888a4-8299-5625-95f0-9f5d0f785306" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I  only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161652/selection/35ffc558ac75968b6d9a8a0179c93d2c14c604859f50a146485ab0309ffdde65" :answer/id #uuid "98dfc48c-f4a7-54d5-bd49-55b4cbac5dc7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III  only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161652/selection/f8bc450b7f4fe2953896918c1f5c69e16edb279ae4186289918e142ef04a634f" :answer/id #uuid "20a76a76-01af-5387-9d46-64dc59b35ceb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II  only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161652/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c683ca29-1db4-5edb-92a8-944119592610" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-161652/selection/061c0582fe9c4fc8f6a2754ba48c864a097431d239f9b07d7f28c26670db035c" :answer-field/choices ["q-161652/selection/061c0582fe9c4fc8f6a2754ba48c864a097431d239f9b07d7f28c26670db035c" "q-161652/selection/f875651f7f1318c0bb7eec422091a285a478534fed6eb95898ab3cf27eb909ff" "q-161652/selection/18f1ea50d5b97ea6ddf4ed047cc851740c3854be5650eb9e76df7f5a3d1456f8" "q-161652/selection/35ffc558ac75968b6d9a8a0179c93d2c14c604859f50a146485ab0309ffdde65" "q-161652/selection/f8bc450b7f4fe2953896918c1f5c69e16edb279ae4186289918e142ef04a634f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-161652" :question/id #uuid "5ee0de30-057d-5ea4-a8b3-df4f777834db" :question/math-academy-id "q-161652" :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,1<{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<4}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?  \n\n- $∂A\\cap A\\ne ∅$\n- $\\text{int}\\,A\\cap ∂A=∅$\n- $A=\\text{int}\\,A$" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nIn this case, the set $A$ and its boundary $∂A={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}$ are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072304/assets/2273cd843c4bfaeaff10d49d3400d7661262673639a66034638d805eef5b1e47.png)\n\n   \n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072304/assets/5e473584ef5193b434ff6c138b08c4fbd9111a37252019143b1afb2d48c913c6.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statement I is false. As we've seen, $A$ contains none of its boundary points, so we must have  $∂A\\cap A=∅.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Since $\\text{int}\\,A$ contains all points in $A$ except the boundary points, we must have $\\text{int}\\,A\\cap ∂A=∅,$ where $∅$ denotes the empty set.\n\n- Statement III is true. Since $A$ contains none of its boundary points, we must have $A=\\text{int}\\,A.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III  only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-161652/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a024c46e-0374-5d03-b895-eb754ff7ad97"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161652"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-161721/selection/3d69fb161280dd11c3f43c5280d08fc90f2b4c7b5778457fc8c3bc48eef0fadd" :answer/id #uuid "719376f3-5fc0-5913-b62f-f66b638d41f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0\\le x\\le 2,\\text{ }0<y<2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161721/selection/632392d55204986c91cc335144ce88c4316aca1657098ae1e14d80e71a85c7ba" :answer/id #uuid "9f9af5b4-9f9a-51a1-8849-24d0dd86db81" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0<x<2,\\text{ }0\\le y\\le 2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161721/selection/6d5f73c0f66671a12519164f1a56f79de845fcd0d02d873f1379034f750b2aeb" :answer/id #uuid "a5d7686d-5e63-5a0f-937e-5f0a359c9a98" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0\\le x<2,\\text{ }0\\le y<2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161721/selection/9a90f20c5835efa264af3326fdf881fec3bb1249d9a0a7bfdf087b6cd1f1bf56" :answer/id #uuid "cc3713ff-d46f-5016-b769-f9378e17ac7d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0<x<2,\\text{ }0<y<2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161721/selection/6a5c609f194e24ccfd5b87e573b4d31e68a677f056509eb216bc5bd9f45ea418" :answer/id #uuid "52a076ea-595b-5982-a2a6-084ca7bb30f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0\\le x\\le 2,\\text{ }0\\le y\\le 2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161721/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b5ad199c-ed02-58fd-ae04-a2f3f15a51a2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-161721/selection/9a90f20c5835efa264af3326fdf881fec3bb1249d9a0a7bfdf08